    "evidence_text": "Cow Creek (Montana)\n\nLithia Springs Creek\n\n It is approximately 3.2 mi long and flows through Point Township.\n\n The watershed of the creek has an area of 8.96 sqmi .\n\n It has a named tributary known as Johnson Creek.\n\n At least one bridge more than 20 ft long crosses the creek.\n\n The creek is considered to be a Coldwater Fishery and a Migratory Fishery.\n\nLocks Creek\n\n It is the largest tributary of Frenchmans Creek, a larger stream.\n\nEast Branch South Fork Eel River\n\n The East Branch is the South Fork Eel's largest tributary.\n\nRed Rock River (Montana)\n\n Its drainage basin covers over 1548 mi2 .\n\nDarling River\n\nFrenchmans Creek (California)\nFrenchmans Creek is a 4.4 mi stream in San Mateo County, California.\n Locks Creek is its largest tributary.\n\nJemez River\n\n The East Fork Jemez River is about 22 mi long.\n\nFrenchmans Creek (New South Wales)\n\nTomichi Creek\n\n At Parlin, Quartz Creek flows from Pitkin and Ohio into Tomichi Creek.\n\n A map can be viewed at the BLM Colorado website here.",
